I left out the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`, and an `http-client` import would add authority the graph doesn't declare. The fetch would also send untrusted feed text in a URL query string to a host outside the node's grant. If the platform team extended the grant, the graph's `with` clause needs updating so the world can import `http-client`. The classification logic below is unchanged and fails closed: an unparseable model reply drops the item.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{feed-item, classification};
    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;
    export run: func(item: feed-item) -> classification;
}
```

